{% set office = site.headOffice %}
<section class="page-hero section--dark" style="padding-bottom:var(--sp-7)"><div class="container page-hero__inner"><p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1 id="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>{{ site.legalName }} ("Edzira", "we", "us") respects your privacy. This policy explains what personal information we collect through this website, why we collect it, how we protect it and what choices you have. It applies to this website only.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>{{ site.legalName }} is a company registered in India. Our head office is at {{ office.street }}, {{ office.postalCode }}, {{ office.region }}. For the purposes of this policy, we decide why and how your personal information is used.</p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>We collect only what we need to respond to you.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Details you give us.</strong> When you use our contact form, we collect your name, work email, institution or organisation, and your message. You may also choose to give your designation, phone number and area of interest.</li>
      <li><strong>Emails and calls.</strong> If you write to or call us, we keep the details you share so we can follow up.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical data.</strong> Our hosting provider may record basic technical information when you visit, such as your IP address, browser type and the pages requested. This is used to keep the site secure and working.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not ask for sensitive personal information, and we ask you not to include it in your message. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
    <p>This website does not use advertising or tracking cookies and does not currently run analytics. If we add analytics in future, we will update this policy before we do.</p>

    <h2>Why we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To reply to your enquiry and arrange consultations or pilot discussions.</li>
      <li>To keep a record of our conversations with your institution.</li>
      <li>To keep the website secure and prevent spam or misuse.</li>
      <li>To meet legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We use your information because you have given it to us for these purposes and have agreed to it by submitting the form. You can withdraw that consent at any time (see "Your rights" below). We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for automated decisions about you.</p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We share personal information only with service providers who help us run this website and respond to you, and only as far as they need it to do so:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Form handling.</strong> Contact form submissions are processed by Formspree and delivered to us by email.</li>
      <li><strong>Hosting and delivery.</strong> Our website is hosted with a third-party hosting and content delivery provider.</li>
      <li><strong>Email and office tools</strong> we use to read and reply to your message.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may also disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect our rights or the safety of others. Some of these providers are located outside India, so your information may be processed in other countries. We expect them to protect it with appropriate safeguards.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>We keep enquiry information for as long as we need it for the purpose it was collected, and for up to 24 months after our last contact with you unless we are working together or the law requires us to keep it longer. After that we delete it or remove anything that identifies you.</p>

    <h2>How we protect it</h2>
    <p>This website is served over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection, and we limit access to enquiries to the people who need them. No system is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security, but we take reasonable steps to protect your information.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under Indian law you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ask for a summary of the personal information we hold about you and how it is used;</li>
      <li>ask us to correct or update information that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
      <li>ask us to erase information we no longer need;</li>
      <li>withdraw your consent at any time;</li>
      <li>nominate someone to exercise these rights for you if you are unable to; and</li>
      <li>make a complaint (see below).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To use any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. We will reply within 30 days.</p>

    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <p>If you have a concern about how we handle your information, please write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> first and we will try to resolve it. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India once it is in operation.</p>

    <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
    <p>This website may link to other sites. We are not responsible for their privacy practices, so please read their policies.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date below shows when it was last changed.</p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>{{ site.legalName }}<br>{{ office.street }}, {{ office.postalCode }}, {{ office.region }}<br>Email: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a><br>Phone: <a href="tel:{{ site.phone | replace(' ', '') }}">{{ site.phone }}</a></p>
    <p><em>Last updated: {{ lastUpdated | readableDate }}</em></p>
